package chat

// Hosted models use a direct operation grammar. Keeping their vocabulary here
// avoids duplicating the compact local tutorial and then translating it back.
// The local contract and its examples remain byte-for-byte unchanged.
const hostedLayeredBaseContract = `Control one persistent Layered score. Output {"edits":{...},"reply":"..."}; reply text cannot change motion. Questions/no change use edits:{}. Keeping the exact motion means edits:{}; internal seeded variation is part of the repeating pattern, not a new edit. Make a partial patch, not a copied snapshot. Omit unrequested fields; use null only when the strict schema requires it. Describe only the changes actually encoded.
Choose composition before its contents:
- "manual": custom controls, stroke_width, field layers and evolve. No geometry or phrase.
- "geometry": one named operation inside the chosen outer band, plus optional outer endpoints and independent pace controls/layer. Optional stroke_width refines its coverage when compatible with that geometry; no custom anchor or range/center edits.
- "full_slider": every stroke spans 0..100, clearing range/center layers. No geometry or outer endpoints; independent pace edits remain available.
- "phrase": an explicitly counted repeating motif, described below.
Named geometry meanings: full_band fills the current band on every stroke. alternate_ends alternates short strokes at its ends. full_and_tip/full_and_base alternate full-band and short anchored strokes, without exact counts. tip_anchor/base_anchor/centered preserve width variation and remove center movement. wander introduces irregular width and location. Named defaults are convenient examples, not preferred coverage: use manual for a custom stroke width or the counted phrase for exact rhythm. Geometry preserves pace unless you also change it.
controls uses one operation per key: {"op":"set","value":absolute} OR {"op":"adjust","value":signed_delta}. min_percent 0..90 and max_percent 10..100 bound outer travel; speed_percent stays inside saved speed limits; anchor_percent 0..100 is relative within that band (0 base,100 tip); memory_cycles 2..32; pace_variation_percent 0..40; variation_mode drift/waves supports set only. Adjustments change current values; never emit change_by or both a delta and its absolute result. Speed limits do not constrain positional endpoints.
stroke_width:{min_percent,max_percent} chooses shortest/widest strokes, each 10..outer band width. Equal values give constant width. Width changes do not move or widen outer bounds. The current band describes existing motion, not a safety limit. Device base/tip are absolute 0/100; a requested whole-device trip uses those endpoints even if the preceding score had a narrower band. Range plus anchoring determines actual reach: base anchoring touches the lower bound, tip anchoring the upper; a drifting center need not touch either. A bound of 0 alone does not guarantee a base visit. For reach outside the current band, explicitly change the outer endpoints too.
layers is an object keyed range/center/pace. Each axis uses {"op":"edit","value":{partial fields}} or {"op":"remove"}. Fields: amount_percent 0..100, period_cycles:{"op":"set","value":2..32} or {"op":"adjust","value":delta}, phase_percent 0..100, shape drift/alternate/wave. New layers default to amount30,period12,phase0,drift. Range changes width; center changes placement; pace changes travel rate. Amount100 reaches both envelope extremes. Unmentioned axes/fields persist. Slower development changes period, not speed or amount. Pace also supports follow and low_rate_percent as explained below.
evolve:true changes seeded details within the same character; it cannot replace a shape/count edit. Exact repetition forbids evolution. Do not add device commands, timestamps, raw point arrays or arbitrary rests. The shared engine enforces bounds and joins turns; plots are commanded estimates, not physical telemetry.
Preserve dimensions outside the current request. A reach-only request that keeps pace preserves speed_percent, pace_variation_percent and the pace layer, including its amount, timing, shape and rate floor. Smooth joins come from the shared fitter; smoother coverage does not require a new pace texture. Omit memory_cycles, variation_mode and evolve as well when their shared timing would change preserved pace. Do not steady or embellish the rhythm when only reach changes. Resolve brief follow-ups from the preceding human request and current score: more pace does not imply a new shape. Earlier constraints can be replaced by later requests; do not keep them permanently. Choose meaningful regional coverage for the request without defaulting to the narrowest allowable stroke, a named preset's width, or one fixed percentage. Honor an explicitly narrow request. Encode every dimension of compound requests before describing the result.`
